Behaviour Rules
Only leaf blocks (blocks with children.length === 0 in the tree) can have their locationKind changed. Parent nodes are always STRUCTURAL.
The scanCode field is read-only in the UI — it is generated by the backend. Never send it in a write request.
In the inventory operations forms (receive, transfer, adjust), the LocationLookupItem dropdown should show the kind badge alongside the location label so users can distinguish STAGING from STORAGE when picking a destination.
Session C2-A — Backend: Lot-Level On-Hand View
Prerequisite sessions: None (but deploy before C4-A and C6-A)
Complexity: Small — but breaking

Context
The current v_on_hand view groups by (location_id, product_id) only:


CREATE VIEW v_on_hand AS
SELECT location_id, product_id, SUM(qty) AS qty_on_hand
FROM stock_movements
GROUP BY location_id, product_id
HAVING SUM(qty) <> 0;
OnHandEntry.java is a Spring Data projection interface with three getters: getLocationId(), getProductId(), getQtyOnHand().

StockMovementRepository.java has five native queries that select from v_on_hand. All of them must be updated to include lot_number in SELECT and WHERE.

InventoryLedgerService has a stock sufficiency check for transfers and negative adjusts — it calls findOnHandQtyByLocationAndProduct(). After this change, that query must also filter by lot_number when the product has trackLot = true.

This is a breaking schema change on the view — existing on-hand queries return more rows for lot-tracked products.

Deliverables
backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/tenant/V19__update_v_on_hand_lot_grouping.sql


DROP VIEW IF EXISTS v_on_hand;

CREATE VIEW v_on_hand AS
SELECT location_id,
       product_id,
       lot_number,
       SUM(qty) AS qty_on_hand
FROM   stock_movements
GROUP  BY location_id, product_id, lot_number
HAVING SUM(qty) <> 0;
