Session C6-A — Backend: Count Sessions
Prerequisite sessions: C2-A, C3-A
Complexity: Large

Context
No count session exists. ADJUST movements exist and will be used for variance posting. The count session workflow: open a session (snapshot expected stock from v_on_hand), workers fill in counted quantities, post (write ADJUST movements only for variances), or void (discard without movements).

The snapshot on open is critical — it captures what the system expected at the moment the session started, even if stock changes afterwards.

All new files under tenant/counting/.

Deliverables
New migration: V23__create_count_sessions.sql


CREATE TABLE count_sessions (
  id           UUID PRIMARY KEY,
  name         VARCHAR(120) NOT NULL,
  status       VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'OPEN',
  created_by   VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  created_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
  posted_at    TIMESTAMPTZ,
  posted_by    VARCHAR(255),
  voided_at    TIMESTAMPTZ,
  voided_by    VARCHAR(255)
);

-- Which locations are covered by this session
CREATE TABLE count_session_locations (
  session_id  UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES count_sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  location_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES layout_blocks(id),
  PRIMARY KEY (session_id, location_id)
);

CREATE TABLE count_lines (
  id             UUID PRIMARY KEY,
  session_id     UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES count_sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  location_id    UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES layout_blocks(id),
  product_id     UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES products(id),
  lot_number     VARCHAR(100),
  expected_qty   NUMERIC(15,4) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  counted_qty    NUMERIC(15,4),  -- NULL until entered by staff
  variance       NUMERIC(15,4) GENERATED ALWAYS AS (counted_qty - expected_qty) STORED
);

CREATE INDEX idx_count_lines_session ON count_lines(session_id);
New files:

tenant/counting/CountStatus.java — enum: OPEN, POSTED, VOID
tenant/counting/CountSession.java
tenant/counting/CountLine.java
tenant/counting/CountSessionRepository.java
tenant/counting/CountLineRepository.java — add findBySessionIdOrderByLocationIdAscProductId(UUID sessionId)
tenant/counting/CountSessionService.java
tenant/counting/CountSessionController.java — base path /{tenantSlug}/count-sessions
CountSessionService method spec:


openSession(name, locationIds: List<UUID>, actor)
  → validate locationIds are all leaf blocks
  → create CountSession with status=OPEN
  → insert rows in count_session_locations
  → snapshot: query v_on_hand WHERE location_id IN (locationIds)
    → for each row: create CountLine(sessionId, locationId, productId, lotNumber, expectedQty=row.qtyOnHand, countedQty=null)
  → for any (location, product, lot) combination in scope that has ZERO on-hand (i.e. not in v_on_hand), do NOT create a line — count lines only represent things currently in stock
  → return session id

updateCountLine(sessionId, lineId, countedQty, actor)
  → validate session is OPEN
  → countedQty must be >= 0
  → update counted_qty on the line

postSession(sessionId, actor)
  → validate OPEN
  → validate ALL lines have counted_qty filled (not null)
  → for each line where variance != 0:
      call inventoryLedgerService.adjust(variance, locationId, productId, lotNumber, sourceDocumentId=sessionId, reasonCode="COUNT_ADJUSTMENT", actor)
  → set status=POSTED
  → @Transactional

voidSession(sessionId, actor)
  → validate OPEN (cannot void after posting)
  → set status=VOID
  → no movements written
Endpoints:


GET    /{tenantSlug}/count-sessions
GET    /{tenantSlug}/count-sessions/{id}
POST   /{tenantSlug}/count-sessions              — openSession
PUT    /{tenantSlug}/count-sessions/{id}/lines/{lid} — updateCountLine
POST   /{tenantSlug}/count-sessions/{id}/post
POST   /{tenantSlug}/count-sessions/{id}/void
Permissions: COUNTING_VIEW, COUNTING_CREATE, COUNTING_POST, COUNTING_VOID

Tests
File: tenant/counting/CountSessionServiceTest.java

