Session C7-A — Backend: Scan Resolver
Prerequisite sessions: C1-A
Complexity: Small

Context
No scan endpoint exists. Product lookup (/inventory/lookups/products) and location lookup (/inventory/lookups/locations) exist as separate paginated searches. A unified resolver is needed for scanner input: one endpoint that takes a raw scanned string and returns what it identifies.

The scan_code column on LayoutBlock was added in C1-A. Product SKU is already unique in the products table.

Deliverables
New files:

tenant/scan/ScanType.java — enum: PRODUCT, LOCATION, LOT
tenant/scan/ScanResolveResult.java — record with type: ScanType, productId?, productSku?, productName?, trackLot?, trackExpiry?, locationId?, locationPathLabel?, locationKind?, scanCode?, lotNumber?
tenant/scan/ScanResolverService.java
tenant/scan/ScanController.java — base path /{tenantSlug}/scan
ScanResolverService.resolve(code: String) logic:

Strip and trim the code
Check products table: WHERE sku = :code AND active = true → if found, return { type: PRODUCT, ... }
Check layout_blocks table: WHERE scan_code = :code → if found, return { type: LOCATION, ... }
Check if code matches pattern {sku}:{lotNumber} (contains exactly one :):
Split on first :
Look up product by sku part
Check stock_movements has any row with (product_id, lot_number) where lot_number = lotNumber part
If both found, return { type: LOT, productId, productSku, productName, lotNumber }
If nothing matches, return 404
Endpoint:


GET /{tenantSlug}/scan/resolve?code={rawCode}
→ 200 ScanResolveResult  |  404 if unresolved
Permission: reuse INVENTORY_VIEW — scan resolution is a read-only lookup.

